; Leg PC -- prefixing alone.  Cautious x block 3, PA's only variable moved.
;
; setprefix(PX_CAU) unprefixes the control range but keeps CR, XON, XOFF,
; DEL, 255 and the packet-start character prefixed (ckcmai.c:2699), and
; re-prefixes XON/XOFF by itself if flow control is ever XON/XOFF (2705).
; So it is safe on this cable without further argument.
;
; Read, in this order:
;
;   1. cmp RCVPC.DAT rcvpc.dat -- byte-exact, or the leg is void.  This is
;      the first change that alters what goes ON THE WIRE, so the failure
;      mode is corruption rather than slowness.
;   2. rxbytes in STEPPC.OUT against PA's.  THIS IS THE ONE THAT SAYS THE
;      MECHANISM ENGAGED.  Round 1 failed here and nowhere else: 37,534
;      against 37,536, two bytes, no effect.  Anything under about 40,000
;      with zero resends means it worked this time.
;   3. rxpeak and rxfull.  Unprefixing raises the FILE bytes produced per
;      WIRE byte, so the foreground does more work per byte drained even
;      though it does less per file byte.  That is a reason to expect
;      rxpeak to RISE, and round 1 already put rxfull at 649 once.

set line /dev/tty.usbserial-ABBFKXM1
set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aePC.pkt
send rcvpc.dat
statistics
